2026-06-30 15:25:57,437 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'timeout': 300, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-edfd63dd-ba72-4a51-9bee-1a3a3259ffda', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are an expert SDRF-Proteomics annotator for crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) datasets.\n\nExtract the following SDRF metadata terms from the provided publication text and/or PRIDE project description.\n\nTERMS TO EXTRACT:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nterm: disease\nsdrf_column: characteristics[disease]\nontology: EFO:0000408, MONDO, DOID, PATO\ndescription: Disease state of the sample.\ninstructions: For healthy/normal samples use "normal" (PATO:0000461). For diseased\n  samples use MONDO or DOID terms. Return null only if completely unstated.\n  Most XL-MS samples are "normal" unless explicitly studying a disease model.\n\nterm: phenotype\nsdrf_column: characteristics[phenotype]\nontology: EFO:0000651, PATO, EFO\ndescription: Observable characteristics or traits (drug sensitivity, molecular markers,\n  expression phenotypes, environmental responses).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated. This captures how the sample behaves/appears\n  (distinct from disease diagnosis).\n\nterm: treatment\nsdrf_column: characteristics[treatment]\nontology: EFO:0000727, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Treatment or perturbation applied to the sample (drug, stimulus,\n  environmental stress, growth condition change).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated or not applicable. Examples: "doxycycline\n  treatment", "heat shock", "DMSO vehicle control".\n\nterm: compound\nsdrf_column: characteristics[compound]\nontology: CHEBI:24431, CHEBI, NCIT, EFO\ndescription: Chemical compound or drug applied to the sample.\ninstructions: Use ChEBI if possible. Return null if no compound treatment. Do NOT\n  include the crosslinking reagent here — that goes in comment[cross-linker].\n\nterm: dose\nsdrf_column: characteristics[dose]\nontology: NCIT:C25488\ndescription: Dose or concentration of compound treatment.\npattern: number + unit (e.g. 10 mg/kg, 50 uM, 100 nM, 10 mg/mL)\ninstructions: Return null if no compound treatment or dose not stated.\n\nterm: genetic modification\nsdrf_column: characteristics[genetic modification]\nontology: EFO:0000510, EFO\ndescription: Method of genetic modification (knockout, knockdown, overexpression,\n  transduction). Describes HOW the modification was done.\ninstructions: Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: perturbation\nsdrf_column: characteristics[perturbation]\nontology: PRIDE:0000700\ndescription: Type of perturbation applied (environmental/experimental perturbation).\ninstructions: Return null if not stated or not applicable.\n\nterm: depletion\nsdrf_column: characteristics[depletion]\nontology: PRIDE:0000020\ndescription: Whether abundant protein depletion was performed.\nallowed_values: no depletion, depletion, not applicable\ninstructions: Return "no depletion" if not mentioned. Return "depletion" if\n  high-abundance protein removal is described (e.g. albumin depletion).\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string, list, or null)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Methods"), or null'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nAPEX2 proximity labeling of PI(3)P dependent ER and early endosome membrane contact tether proteins\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nTo understand the nature of ER and early endosome membrane contact site, we capitalized the MTM1 knock out (KO) HeLa cells that do not dissociate the ER and early endosome membrane contact upon nutrient starvation. By using the Doxycyclin inducible APEX2 fused Rab5A (early endosome marker) expressing stable cell lines of wildtype (WT) or KO cells, early endsome proximity proteins were acutely biotinyated during starvation. Subsequent biochemical fractionation were conducted to enrich ER membrane and biotinylated proteins were furhter enriched for Mass spectrometry analysis.\n\n[METHODS]\nHeLa WT or MTM1 KO cell line stably expressing doxycycline-inducible 3xHA-APEX2-Rab5A were seeded in 15 cm dishes with 17x10^5 cells (WT=6 dishes, KO=3 dishes) in the presence of doxycycline for 16 h prior to biotinylation. The next day cells at approximately 85% confluency were starved (EBSS, 2hr) and treated with 500 μM phenol-biotin and hydrogen peroxide to induce biotinylation, quenched, washed once with isolation buffer (225 mM mannitol, 75 mM sucrose, 30 mM Tris-HCl pH 7.4, 0.1 mM EGTA), and, finally, scraped into 1 ml of the same buffer resulting in approx. 2 ml total volume. 0.5 ml of this sample were saved (whole cell lysate, WCL) as a control. The remaining 1.5ml were homogenized using a 2 ml dounce homogenizer (approx. 100-120 strokes) on ice in the presence of protease and phosphatase inhibitors. To isolate light membranes containing the ER, the material was centrifuged twice at 600xg for 2 min each. The pellet (F1) including nuclei and cell debris was resuspended in 150 μl RIPA buffer. The remaining supernatant was centrifuged twice at 7,000xg for 20 min each. The resulting pellet (F2) including the mitochondrial fraction was resuspended in 150 μl RIPA buffer and further fractionated by centrifugation at 20,000xg for 60 min to pellet light ER membranes (F3). This ER-enriched membrane fraction was resuspended in150 μl RIPA buffer. Protein concentration was determined using the Bradford assay. To isolate biotinylated proteins, 130 μg of WCL or F3 fraction were rotated in the presence of Streptavidin Magnetic Beads. Eluted biotinylated proteins were reduced (5mM DTT, 30 min at 55°C), alkylated (15mM iodacetamide, 20 min at RT in the dark) and were submitted to LC-MS analysis (Samples from two independent experiments).\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
